## 3.4 Password management

Every executive must be able to change their own password.

Create:

Executive Dashboard → Profile & Security → Change Password.

Fields:

- Current password.
- New password.
- Confirm new password.

Provide an eye icon to show or hide the characters currently being typed.

Do not reveal an existing stored password.

Use secure salted password hashing.

Do not store passwords in plaintext.

Require a new password when an officer activates their account.

## 3.5 Password visibility

Both member and executive password inputs should have a show/hide password control.

This is intended to help users verify what they are typing.

Do not create a feature that retrieves a stored password from the database.

Passwords are hashed and should not be reversible.

If login fails, display a clear message that the username or password is incorrect.

